WEBVTT

00:00:00.043 --> 00:00:01.044 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Builder.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Blueprint.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:04.074 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson one.

00:00:04.626 --> 00:00:05.355 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Introduction.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:07.616 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Education only.

00:00:08.175 --> 00:00:09.489 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not financial advice.

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:12.061 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information and

00:00:12.061 --> 00:00:14.264 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:16.164 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
financial situation or needs.

00:00:16.684 --> 00:00:18.883 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto, a digital coin, is high risk;

00:00:18.883 --> 00:00:21.319 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you could lose all the money you put in.

00:00:21.839 --> 00:00:23.904 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:23.904 --> 00:00:25.613 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
indicator of future results.

00:00:26.663 --> 00:00:29.056 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The prices are public historical prices

00:00:29.056 --> 00:00:31.234 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
at the end of each day, marked Example.

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.266 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:00:35.265 --> 00:00:37.241 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end of this series you will

00:00:37.241 --> 00:00:39.291 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
understand what a grid bot, a small

00:00:39.291 --> 00:00:41.340 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
program that places these orders

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.243 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for you, does, when it can capture

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:44.854 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bounces, and where it loses.

00:00:45.374 --> 00:00:47.384 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will know how to plan one, test

00:00:47.384 --> 00:00:49.284 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
it on paper, run it, check it, and

00:00:49.284 --> 00:00:51.331 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
change the capital you give to bots

00:00:51.331 --> 00:00:53.193 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
only under written risk rules.

00:00:53.713 --> 00:00:55.110 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is education, not

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.429 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a promise of results.

00:00:56.949 --> 00:00:58.560 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Price often moves sideways,

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.310 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bouncing between the same top

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:02.061 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and bottom instead of leaving.

00:01:02.581 --> 00:01:04.290 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid is a ladder of waiting

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.000 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
orders, called limit orders,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.487 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
built for that bouncing.

00:01:08.007 --> 00:01:09.850 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
When price runs one way and stays

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:12.029 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
there, the grid has nothing left to do.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.163 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
And if price falls through the

00:01:14.163 --> 00:01:15.846 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bottom, coin means the crypto

00:01:15.846 --> 00:01:17.669 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
itself, and you are left holding

00:01:17.669 --> 00:01:19.401 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the coin, and it is worth less.

00:01:20.331 --> 00:01:21.672 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end you will know

00:01:21.672 --> 00:01:22.957 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
what a grid bot places.

00:01:24.086 --> 00:01:26.165 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will see that idea on

00:01:26.165 --> 00:01:28.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
one real path from 2023.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.848 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will be able to say the

00:01:30.848 --> 00:01:32.301 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stop rule in one sentence.

00:01:33.255 --> 00:01:35.101 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
When a chart says Example, it

00:01:35.101 --> 00:01:36.946 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
means a real past price used

00:01:36.946 --> 00:01:38.792 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
as an example, not a forecast.

00:01:39.842 --> 00:01:41.084 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is a digital

00:01:41.084 --> 00:01:42.481 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
asset, such as bitcoin.

00:01:43.001 --> 00:01:44.677 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not need to have bought

00:01:44.677 --> 00:01:45.962 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
any before this lesson.

00:01:46.341 --> 00:01:48.308 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange is the website or app

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:50.640 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
where you swap Australian dollars for

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.681 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto, and crypto back to dollars.

00:01:53.201 --> 00:01:54.877 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course does not name one,

00:01:54.877 --> 00:01:56.553 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and it does not send an order.

00:01:57.298 --> 00:01:58.862 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Cash is money you can spend.

00:01:59.264 --> 00:02:00.886 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here that means dollars, or a

00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:02.650 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollar-pegged token, treated

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:04.060 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
like cash in this lesson.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:05.596 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The peg can break.

00:02:06.116 --> 00:02:08.308 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Coin is the crypto, such as bitcoin.

00:02:09.358 --> 00:02:11.704 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order is an instruction to buy or sell.

00:02:12.156 --> 00:02:13.964 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A buy order swaps cash for coin.

00:02:14.484 --> 00:02:16.386 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A sell order swaps coin back to

00:02:16.386 --> 00:02:18.518 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cash, and you can only sell coin you

00:02:18.518 --> 00:02:20.420 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
already hold, on a spot account.

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:23.240 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot is software that places

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.862 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and refills orders for you.

00:02:25.382 --> 00:02:27.226 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You start with some cash and some

00:02:27.226 --> 00:02:28.902 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
coin, so there is something to

00:02:28.902 --> 00:02:30.633 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
buy with and something to sell.

00:02:30.682 --> 00:02:33.047 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid bot places waiting buy orders

00:02:33.047 --> 00:02:35.175 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on lines below the price and sell

00:02:35.175 --> 00:02:37.304 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
orders on lines above it, inside a

00:02:37.304 --> 00:02:39.038 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
top and a bottom you choose.

00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:41.234 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The space between your top and

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:42.966 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your bottom is called the band.

00:02:43.075 --> 00:02:45.180 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sells need some coin, so a grid

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.130 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
starts with part cash and part

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:49.079 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
coin, and that is a description,

00:02:49.079 --> 00:02:50.951 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not advice about what to hold.

00:02:52.001 --> 00:02:53.707 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A limit order is an order that

00:02:53.707 --> 00:02:55.271 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waits at a price you choose.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.355 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not chase the price.

00:02:57.774 --> 00:02:59.338 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Chasing the price would mean

00:02:59.338 --> 00:03:00.791 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
moving the order to follow

00:03:00.791 --> 00:03:02.355 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wherever the price has gone.

00:03:03.204 --> 00:03:05.279 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order fills when the price reaches

00:03:05.279 --> 00:03:07.011 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
its line and the trade happens.

00:03:07.473 --> 00:03:09.679 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Until then, the order is only waiting.

00:03:10.729 --> 00:03:12.685 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Think of a ladder leaned on a wall.

00:03:12.826 --> 00:03:15.172 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The rungs wait, and they do not chase you.

00:03:15.448 --> 00:03:17.739 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A rung is one price where an order waits.

00:03:18.146 --> 00:03:20.324 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The gap is the space between two rungs.

00:03:20.614 --> 00:03:22.658 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The ladder is the analogy, and the

00:03:22.658 --> 00:03:24.930 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
chart beside it is the real past path.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.390 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The range is the top rung

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:28.519 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the bottom rung.

00:03:29.039 --> 00:03:31.162 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The levels are the rungs between them.

00:03:31.512 --> 00:03:33.802 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop is the written rule for leaving.

00:03:34.651 --> 00:03:36.495 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The range is the top line and the

00:03:36.495 --> 00:03:38.339 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bottom line, taken from the path.

00:03:38.817 --> 00:03:40.305 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Hindsight: this range is

00:03:40.305 --> 00:03:41.570 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
drawn after the fact.

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:45.314 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The chart is bitcoin's real daily

00:03:45.314 --> 00:03:48.884 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closes from 19 July to 16 October 2023.

00:03:49.404 --> 00:03:50.857 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every close in this window

00:03:50.857 --> 00:03:52.588 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stayed between those two lines.

00:03:53.374 --> 00:03:55.780 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Six gaps of about 900 dollars each sit

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:58.341 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
between the bottom line and the top line.

00:03:58.861 --> 00:04:01.088 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each gap is about 900 dollars:

00:04:01.088 --> 00:04:03.315 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the top line minus the bottom

00:04:03.315 --> 00:04:04.800 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
line, divided by six.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:06.655 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is one step between

00:04:06.655 --> 00:04:08.138 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lines, not the whole band.

00:04:08.658 --> 00:04:10.497 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Seven lines make those six gaps.

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.804 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The levels are the prices on the

00:04:12.804 --> 00:04:14.480 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
rungs where limit orders wait.

00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:17.758 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Buy orders wait on lines below the price.

00:04:18.193 --> 00:04:20.149 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Sell orders wait on lines above it.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:23.129 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each fill changes what you hold: a buy

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:25.795 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fill adds coin, and a sell fill adds cash.

00:04:26.315 --> 00:04:27.433 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You choose the band,

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:28.717 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the gaps and the money.

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:30.454 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The bot places each order.

00:04:31.461 --> 00:04:33.253 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
After a fill, the bot places the

00:04:33.253 --> 00:04:34.974 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
opposite order one rung away.

00:04:35.494 --> 00:04:37.673 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A buy fill gets a sell one rung higher.

00:04:38.059 --> 00:04:40.289 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A sell fill gets a buy one rung lower.

00:04:40.809 --> 00:04:42.429 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You still write the stop, and

00:04:42.429 --> 00:04:44.105 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you act when that rule is met.

00:04:44.337 --> 00:04:46.571 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The bot does not decide the stop for you

00:04:46.571 --> 00:04:48.694 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
unless you turned that setting on, and

00:04:48.694 --> 00:04:50.761 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you write which one before you start.

00:04:51.496 --> 00:04:52.836 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Think of a market stall.

00:04:53.268 --> 00:04:55.383 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stallholder buys stock a little

00:04:55.383 --> 00:04:57.497 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cheaper and sells it a little dearer,

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:59.117 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and pays a fee on every sale.

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:01.136 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Exchanges charge a small

00:05:01.136 --> 00:05:02.183 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fee on each trade.

00:05:02.703 --> 00:05:04.430 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid can do that while price

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:05.870 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bounces inside the band.

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:08.911 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bounce means price moves down and back

00:05:08.911 --> 00:05:11.280 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
up, or up and back down, and stays inside.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.036 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One buy at a lower line and the later

00:05:14.036 --> 00:05:16.119 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sell of that same coin is one pair.

00:05:16.639 --> 00:05:18.791 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On these daily closes, the July to

00:05:18.791 --> 00:05:21.023 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
October example window finished

00:05:21.023 --> 00:05:23.095 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
only three pairs one rung apart.

00:05:23.615 --> 00:05:25.347 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sell line is higher, so the

00:05:25.347 --> 00:05:27.191 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cash that comes back is more than

00:05:27.191 --> 00:05:29.146 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the cash that left, before the fee.

00:05:29.439 --> 00:05:30.892 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A fee is what the exchange

00:05:30.892 --> 00:05:32.456 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
charges when an order fills.

00:05:32.637 --> 00:05:34.257 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The fee comes out of the gap.

00:05:34.484 --> 00:05:36.216 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the fees are larger than the

00:05:36.216 --> 00:05:37.780 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
gap, the pair keeps nothing.

00:05:37.961 --> 00:05:39.204 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is not a promise.

00:05:39.724 --> 00:05:41.528 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair finishes only if price

00:05:41.528 --> 00:05:43.401 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
does bounce and both orders fill.

00:05:44.451 --> 00:05:45.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The daily close is the

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:46.909 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
last price of the day.

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:49.130 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto trades all day, so the

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:50.539 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
day is cut at a set time.

00:05:51.059 --> 00:05:54.069 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The exchange's day starts at 11am Sydney

00:05:54.069 --> 00:05:56.990 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
time in daylight saving, 10am otherwise.

00:05:57.510 --> 00:05:59.494 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is a simple candle that shows

00:05:59.494 --> 00:06:01.170 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the day's high, low and close.

00:06:01.644 --> 00:06:03.573 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Traders call it a candle because

00:06:03.573 --> 00:06:05.502 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the full version has a thick body

00:06:05.502 --> 00:06:07.234 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and a thin wick, like a candle.

00:06:07.666 --> 00:06:09.174 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here we only need the high,

00:06:09.174 --> 00:06:10.403 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the low and the close.

00:06:10.737 --> 00:06:13.917 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This candle is 19 July 2023.

00:06:14.437 --> 00:06:15.666 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The high, the low, and

00:06:15.666 --> 00:06:16.951 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the close are labelled.

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:19.973 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The example is Bitcoin's public

00:06:19.973 --> 00:06:21.629 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily price in US dollars.

00:06:22.149 --> 00:06:25.347 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
From 19 July 2023 to 16 October

00:06:25.347 --> 00:06:28.290 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
2023, every one of those days

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:30.722 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closed inside the band.

00:06:31.242 --> 00:06:32.915 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The close crossed the seven

00:06:32.915 --> 00:06:34.661 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lines 28 times in that window.

00:06:35.181 --> 00:06:37.492 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The count is an example, not a forecast.

00:06:38.012 --> 00:06:39.800 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
We do not need to read each day.

00:06:40.066 --> 00:06:41.409 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The shape is the lesson,

00:06:41.409 --> 00:06:42.822 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and it is marked Example.

00:06:43.342 --> 00:06:46.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Worked check: 19 July

00:06:46.098 --> 00:06:49.179 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
2023 to 16 October 2023.

00:06:49.699 --> 00:06:51.207 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The low is the bottom line.

00:06:51.687 --> 00:06:53.153 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The high is the top line.

00:06:53.673 --> 00:06:55.517 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Nothing on this card is an order.

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:59.323 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Those 28 crossings, each time the price

00:06:59.323 --> 00:07:01.722 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crosses a line, are not 28 results.

00:07:02.242 --> 00:07:04.444 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A crossing only means the close moved

00:07:04.444 --> 00:07:06.511 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
from one side of a line to the other.

00:07:06.953 --> 00:07:08.665 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A pair is finished only when a

00:07:08.665 --> 00:07:10.519 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
buy and its later sell have both

00:07:10.519 --> 00:07:12.250 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled, and only after the fee.

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:14.649 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The price can cross many lines and

00:07:14.649 --> 00:07:16.549 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
still leave you holding coin if it

00:07:16.549 --> 00:07:18.169 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
walks out through the bottom.

00:07:18.705 --> 00:07:20.214 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You can buy part of a coin.

00:07:20.763 --> 00:07:23.722 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here we buy one hundredth

00:07:23.763 --> 00:07:24.824 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of a bitcoin, 0.01.

00:07:24.824 --> 00:07:27.788 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In this example a buy waiting at the

00:07:27.788 --> 00:07:31.077 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lower of these two lines was reached on

00:07:31.077 --> 00:07:34.059 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
17 August 2023, and the sell one line

00:07:34.059 --> 00:07:37.040 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
above was reached on 29 August 2023.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.347 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The card shows the gap, then the

00:07:39.347 --> 00:07:40.912 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
two fees, then what is left.

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:43.045 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That is about 8 dollars 46

00:07:43.045 --> 00:07:45.130 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
after fees, for one small pair.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:47.550 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It happens only if the price comes

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:49.226 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
back up through the sell line.

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.061 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the price leaves through the

00:07:51.061 --> 00:07:52.849 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bottom, you still hold the coin,

00:07:52.849 --> 00:07:54.413 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the pair never finishes.

00:07:54.606 --> 00:07:56.393 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This card is not money you made.

00:07:56.791 --> 00:07:59.138 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Past results don't predict future results.

00:08:06.126 --> 00:08:07.914 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Now watch what you hold when the

00:08:07.914 --> 00:08:09.925 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price leaves the band and stays out.

00:08:10.188 --> 00:08:11.808 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Above the band the sells have

00:08:11.808 --> 00:08:13.596 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled and you are holding cash,

00:08:13.596 --> 00:08:15.048 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with nothing left to sell.

00:08:15.453 --> 00:08:17.017 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Below the band the buys have

00:08:17.017 --> 00:08:18.469 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled and you are holding

00:08:18.469 --> 00:08:20.201 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
coin, with nothing left to buy.

00:08:20.484 --> 00:08:21.876 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That is why the way down

00:08:21.876 --> 00:08:23.634 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
matters most: every buy fills,

00:08:23.634 --> 00:08:25.393 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and you are left holding coin.

00:08:27.443 --> 00:08:29.677 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here is that stop rule on the real path.

00:08:30.098 --> 00:08:32.459 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It triggers if a daily close is outside

00:08:32.459 --> 00:08:34.746 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the band, through the top or the bottom,

00:08:34.746 --> 00:08:37.254 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still outside.

00:08:37.774 --> 00:08:39.227 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then the idea is finished.

00:08:39.607 --> 00:08:41.701 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You stop the bot, which cancels the

00:08:41.701 --> 00:08:43.570 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waiting orders, and do what you

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:45.664 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wrote: keep the coin or swap to cash.

00:08:46.184 --> 00:08:48.165 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot's automatic stop is a price

00:08:48.165 --> 00:08:49.853 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that can fire during the day.

00:08:50.373 --> 00:08:52.073 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course uses the two daily

00:08:52.073 --> 00:08:53.909 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closes, unless your written plan

00:08:53.909 --> 00:08:55.696 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
says you turned on a price stop.

00:08:56.128 --> 00:08:57.469 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is a teaching rule,

00:08:57.469 --> 00:08:58.647 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not a recommendation.

00:08:59.167 --> 00:09:00.787 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop is your written rule

00:09:00.787 --> 00:09:02.239 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for when you stop the bot.

00:09:02.472 --> 00:09:04.606 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On 23 October 2023 the close

00:09:04.606 --> 00:09:07.018 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
finished above the top line, and

00:09:07.018 --> 00:09:09.337 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the next day was still above it.

00:09:14.387 --> 00:09:15.840 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Through the top, the sells

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.516 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
have filled and you hold cash.

00:09:17.624 --> 00:09:19.468 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Through the bottom, the buys have

00:09:19.468 --> 00:09:21.312 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled and you hold coin that you

00:09:21.312 --> 00:09:23.323 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bought above where the price is now.

00:09:23.682 --> 00:09:25.134 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That loss can keep growing

00:09:25.134 --> 00:09:26.252 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
until the stop acts.

00:09:26.557 --> 00:09:28.400 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You stop the bot either way, then

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:29.964 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you follow the written rule.

00:09:30.074 --> 00:09:31.861 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The bot does not decide the stop

00:09:31.861 --> 00:09:33.761 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
unless you turned that setting on.

00:09:34.033 --> 00:09:35.455 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
EXAMPLE, made up: three

00:09:35.455 --> 00:09:37.034 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
buys fill on the way down.

00:09:37.554 --> 00:09:40.854 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One hundredth of a bitcoin

00:09:40.854 --> 00:09:44.153 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
at 27,630 is 276 dollars 30.

00:09:45.008 --> 00:09:50.541 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One hundredth at 26,730 is 267 dollars 30.

00:09:51.393 --> 00:09:56.575 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One hundredth at 25,830 is 258 dollars 30.

00:09:57.095 --> 00:09:59.735 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Together that is 801 dollars 90.

00:10:00.255 --> 00:10:02.431 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A little below the band, at a

00:10:02.431 --> 00:10:04.805 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
made-up price of 24,000, that

00:10:04.805 --> 00:10:06.882 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
coin is worth 720 dollars.

00:10:07.402 --> 00:10:09.028 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You are down 81 dollars 90

00:10:09.028 --> 00:10:10.964 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
before fees, and the loss keeps

00:10:10.964 --> 00:10:12.822 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
growing until your stop acts.

00:10:13.872 --> 00:10:15.447 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A common mistake is thinking

00:10:15.447 --> 00:10:16.956 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot predicts the price.

00:10:17.744 --> 00:10:18.494 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not.

00:10:19.061 --> 00:10:19.843 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It only waits.

00:10:20.212 --> 00:10:21.721 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Another mistake is starting

00:10:21.721 --> 00:10:22.894 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with no written stop.

00:10:23.309 --> 00:10:24.538 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
There is no promise of

00:10:24.538 --> 00:10:25.823 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
results in this lesson.

00:10:26.014 --> 00:10:27.622 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Numbers marked Example are

00:10:27.622 --> 00:10:29.299 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
teaching numbers, not advice.

00:10:30.349 --> 00:10:32.613 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper or demo trading is like driving

00:10:32.613 --> 00:10:34.585 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with learner plates, or training

00:10:34.585 --> 00:10:36.629 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wheels: you practise with pretend

00:10:36.629 --> 00:10:38.455 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
money before anything is real.

00:10:38.975 --> 00:10:40.492 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 7 shows you how.

00:10:41.549 --> 00:10:42.676 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Steps one to six.

00:10:43.376 --> 00:10:45.064 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This introduction is step one.

00:10:45.764 --> 00:10:46.825 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then what you need.

00:10:47.455 --> 00:10:48.983 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then exactly what a grid

00:10:48.983 --> 00:10:50.434 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bot does, order by order.

00:10:51.433 --> 00:10:52.550 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then market regimes.

00:10:53.127 --> 00:10:55.194 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then choosing grid spacing and range.

00:10:55.833 --> 00:10:57.439 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then entry and exit rules.

00:10:58.155 --> 00:10:59.455 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Steps seven to eleven.

00:11:00.155 --> 00:11:01.239 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then a paper test.

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:03.021 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then weekly checks.

00:11:03.758 --> 00:11:04.947 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then common mistakes.

00:11:05.647 --> 00:11:07.658 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then scaling up under written rules.

00:11:08.118 --> 00:11:09.509 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then an opt-in lesson on

00:11:09.509 --> 00:11:11.595 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
liquidation and your complete plan.

00:11:12.645 --> 00:11:14.544 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The next lesson is a checklist you

00:11:14.544 --> 00:11:16.444 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
write on paper, before any screen.

00:11:17.465 --> 00:11:19.842 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In short: a grid waits, it buys lower and

00:11:19.842 --> 00:11:22.219 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sells higher while price bounces, the

00:11:22.219 --> 00:11:24.519 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fees come out of the gap, and if a daily

00:11:24.519 --> 00:11:26.973 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close leaves and stays out, you stop the

00:11:26.973 --> 00:11:29.043 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bot and follow the rule you wrote.

00:11:30.127 --> 00:11:30.993 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check yourself.

00:11:31.513 --> 00:11:32.966 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Why does a grid start with

00:11:32.966 --> 00:11:34.418 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
some coin as well as cash?

00:11:34.582 --> 00:11:35.867 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Because the sell orders

00:11:35.867 --> 00:11:37.375 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
need coin you already hold.

00:11:38.393 --> 00:11:41.114 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the example pair, why is the net about

00:11:41.114 --> 00:11:43.410 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
8 dollars 46 and not the whole gap?

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:45.494 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The two fees come out first.

00:11:46.657 --> 00:11:48.724 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Price closes above your top line, and

00:11:48.724 --> 00:11:50.903 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the next day's close is still above it.

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:52.998 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
What do you do, and who does it?

00:11:53.319 --> 00:11:55.106 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You stop the bot and follow your

00:11:55.106 --> 00:11:56.950 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
written rule, by hand, unless you

00:11:56.950 --> 00:11:58.794 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
turned on the bot's stop setting.

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:00.600 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Your turn.

00:12:01.047 --> 00:12:02.778 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On paper, write the top and the

00:12:02.778 --> 00:12:04.734 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bottom, one gap, and the stop rule.

00:12:05.837 --> 00:12:07.569 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Say what you will do if a daily

00:12:07.569 --> 00:12:09.189 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close leaves the band and the

00:12:09.189 --> 00:12:10.753 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
next close is still outside.

00:12:11.085 --> 00:12:12.481 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Pause the video and write

00:12:12.481 --> 00:12:14.101 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your answer before you go on.

00:12:15.134 --> 00:12:17.201 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No real order is sent in this lesson.

00:12:17.688 --> 00:12:19.591 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper practice comes in Lesson

00:12:19.591 --> 00:12:21.202 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
7, and real money only after

00:12:21.202 --> 00:12:23.031 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your written graduation rule.

00:12:23.551 --> 00:12:25.558 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A graduation rule is the written

00:12:25.558 --> 00:12:27.268 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
test you pass on paper first.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:28.810 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You draw the idea.

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:31.123 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a screen appears later, it

00:12:31.123 --> 00:12:32.839 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
should be a copy of the page,

00:12:32.839 --> 00:12:34.398 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and only on paper or demo.

00:12:35.598 --> 00:12:37.959 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring a notebook, and no secrets: no

00:12:37.959 --> 00:12:40.573 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
seed phrase, private key or API secret.

00:12:41.093 --> 00:12:43.154 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An API secret is a secret key that

00:12:43.154 --> 00:12:45.443 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lets software control your account.

00:12:46.493 --> 00:12:48.186 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair, in the next lesson,

00:12:48.186 --> 00:12:49.801 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
is the two things you swap,

00:12:49.801 --> 00:12:51.570 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
like bitcoin and US dollars.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:54.453 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid bot places waiting buys

00:12:54.453 --> 00:12:56.506 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
below the price and waiting sells

00:12:56.506 --> 00:12:58.486 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
above it, inside a band you choose.

00:12:59.686 --> 00:13:00.804 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A finished pair buys

00:13:00.804 --> 00:13:02.088 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lower and sells higher.

00:13:02.295 --> 00:13:03.915 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The fees come out of the gap.

00:13:04.204 --> 00:13:06.262 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the example that was about 8

00:13:06.262 --> 00:13:08.485 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars 46, and it is not a promise.

00:13:09.685 --> 00:13:11.081 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave through the top and

00:13:11.081 --> 00:13:12.255 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you hold mostly cash.

00:13:12.704 --> 00:13:14.045 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave through the bottom

00:13:14.045 --> 00:13:15.441 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and you hold mostly coin.

00:13:16.483 --> 00:13:18.720 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a daily close leaves the band and the

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:20.818 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
next close is still outside, you stop

00:13:20.818 --> 00:13:22.941 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot and follow the rule you wrote.

00:13:24.115 --> 00:13:26.350 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson: What you are going to need.

00:13:26.739 --> 00:13:28.303 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring your notes: your band,

00:13:28.303 --> 00:13:29.923 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your gaps and your stop rule.

00:13:30.196 --> 00:13:31.554 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep the word Example on

00:13:31.554 --> 00:13:32.844 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every practice figure.

00:13:33.364 --> 00:13:35.319 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson you will write the page

00:13:35.319 --> 00:13:37.330 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of what you need, before any screen.

